  "bio": "Born in the City of Four Elements, Kaldaran always carried a quiet weight. His dreams were plagued by flickers of forgotten rituals, elemental screams, and scorched stone — memories too fractured to name.\n\nHe sought answers in structure. He entered a formal arcane college. His instructors warned against necromancy. Kaldaran was drawn to it anyway — not for power, not for fear, but because the dead remembered what the living forgot.\n\nFor decades he toiled in the tower, always adjacent to knowledge, never invited into it. Until a misfiled scroll triggered a vision: flames, betrayal, and a cracked keystone. Something he may have helped break.\n\nBRUG — THE DEBT OF FREEDOM\nAn ogre bound by a warlock's pact, wearing an iron band he did not know was a mark of ownership. Kaldaran recognized the runes, broke the enchantment, and asked for nothing.\n\nBrug knelt beside the slender wizard and said only: \"Mine now. You saved Brug. Brug smash anything hurt you.\"\n\nHe does not remember who he was. But he remembers that he failed. And this time, he will not look away.",
